node_modules/
dist/
# 🔴 Anchored. An unanchored `fixtures/` matches a directory of that name at
# **any depth**, so it also hid `test/fixtures/` -- four small committed
# reference files that `test/nonbonded-reference.test.ts` and
# `test/triclinic.test.ts` require and that one of them asserts the presence of.
# They were never added, so 10 tests failed on every clone of this repository
# and passed here, which is the shape of every bug in this file: a working tree
# has the file and a clone does not. Found by cloning into /tmp and running
# `npm ci && npm run check`, which is what CI does and what no amount of local
# testing reproduces.
/fixtures/
test-results/
playwright-report/
vendor/openmm-wasm/
*.dcd
*.rst
*.prmtop
*.inpcrd
# Run outputs, which land wherever a tool is invoked. Deliberately unanchored,
# so mind that a *committed* fixture must not be named exactly one of these.
system.xml
state.xml
system.pdb
__pycache__/
.DS_Store
.vite/
*.npy
# Chemical Component Dictionary downloads; the ligand route fetches
# <CODE>.cif and 24 of them were committed to the repository root once.
# Anchored for the reason above: the ligand route writes <CODE>.cif into the
# working directory, and an unanchored rule would also hide a committed one.
/*.cif
